Here's a slider you can drag: change the flash rate, and the count for a 12-second stretch updates immediately.

```openui lifecycle=resumable id=stage-light-flash-rate

root = LearningSurface([sim], "Stage light flash rate", "Drag the rate to change how many flashes occur in 12 seconds.", "resumable")
sim = Simulation("flash-sim", "Flashes in 12 seconds", [
  { id: "rate", label: "Flash rate", unit: "flashes/second", min: 1, max: 20, step: 1, value: 6 }
], [
  { id: "total", label: "Flashes in 12 seconds", unit: "flashes", expr: "rate * 12", precision: 0, emphasis: true },
  { id: "gap", label: "Time between flashes", unit: "seconds", expr: "1 / rate", precision: 3 }
], "resumable", "Start by predicting how many flashes you would get at 10 flashes per second, then move the slider and check.")
```

Try 10 flashes per second first and see whether the count matches your expectation.

