I'll set up a control you can drag: the flash rate, with the count over 12 seconds updating live.

```openui lifecycle=ephemeral id=flash-rate-sim
root = LearningSurface([sim], "Flashes in 12 seconds", "Drag the flash rate and watch the 12-second total update.", "ephemeral")
sim = Simulation("flash-sim", "Stage light flash counter", [
  { id: "rate", label: "Flash rate", unit: "flashes per second", min: 0, max: 20, step: 1, value: 6 }
], [
  { id: "total", label: "Flashes in 12 seconds", unit: "flashes", expr: "rate * 12", emphasis: true },
  { id: "perSecond", label: "Flashes per second", unit: "flashes/s", expr: "rate" }
], "ephemeral", "Move the flash rate slider and watch how the number of flashes in 12 seconds changes. The first slider is the one you asked to change; the totals recalculate immediately.")
```

The starting point is your 6 flashes per second, which gives 72 flashes in 12 seconds. Move the slider to any rate you like and the total follows.

