content.text:
Here's a model where you set the drip flow and watch the 6-minute bucket total.

```openui lifecycle=ephemeral id=drip-irrigation-sim

root = LearningSurface([sim], "Drip irrigation: flow to bucket", "Set the drip flow rate and read the 6-minute bucket total.", "ephemeral")
sim = Simulation("drip-sim", "Flow to bucket over 6 minutes", [
  { id: "flow", label: "Drip flow rate", unit: "L/min", min: 0.5, max: 20, step: 0.5, value: 2 }
], [
  { id: "bucket", label: "Water in bucket", unit: "L", expr: "flow * 6", precision: 1, emphasis: true },
  { id: "rate", label: "Flow rate", unit: "L/min", expr: "flow", precision: 1 }
], "ephemeral", "Move the flow slider. The bucket line reads flow × 6 minutes, assuming no losses to evaporation or runoff. Press Share what I found to send your settings back.")
```

Drag the slider and watch the bucket total scale linearly — every 0.5 L/min adds 3 L over the 6 minutes.

